INT. NIGHT FERRY - CAR DECK - NIGHT

Rows of idling vans and trucks. Rain drumming on the steel hull. A panel truck marked "ST. EMERIC FLORIST" sits near the stern. Its back doors are open.

PETRA SOKOLOV (40s, crew boss, fisherman's sweater) sits on the bumper counting a cashier's envelope. A man in a delivery uniform leans on the truck beside her: THE COURIER (30s, calm, wet hair). DESHAWN "DEE" KARIMI (20s, hacker, laptop on a milk crate) crouches beside them.

PETRA
We got half.

COURIER
That's all there was.

PETRA
You told us twice that.

COURIER
Because I was told twice that.

DEE
The vault logs show a full transfer.

COURIER
The vault logs show what the vault wanted you to see.

PETRA
Who told you that?

COURIER
A man named Hendricks.

DEE
Hendricks is dead.

COURIER
Then he lied last.

PETRA
We didn't kill Hendricks.

DEE
Nobody said we did.

COURIER
Somebody did.

PETRA
Dee, close the laptop.

DEE
I'm trying to trace the other half.

PETRA
Close it.

Dee shuts it slowly. The ferry horn sounds, low and long.

PETRA (CONT'D)
So let me say this plainly. You knew the take was half before we boarded.

COURIER
I suspected.

PETRA
You suspected, and you let us board.

COURIER
You'd have boarded anyway.

DEE
We would have.

PETRA
Don't help him.

DEE
I'm just being honest.

PETRA
Be honest quieter.

PETRA
What do we call you, anyway?

COURIER
Silas.

SILAS
I'll give you what I have. Fifty thousand. In the glove box.

PETRA
That's a tip.

SILAS
It's what's left.

DEE
Petra, take it. We get off at Lindqvist Pier in ten minutes.

PETRA
We're not taking it.

DEE
Why not?

PETRA
Because I'm done being the one who takes less.

SILAS
Then you take nothing.

PETRA
Then I take nothing. But you walk off first.

SILAS
I walk off alone.

PETRA
You walk off alone.

The ferry horn again. Rain on steel. The Courier nods, pulls his collar up, and steps out into the dark of the car deck. Dee stares after him. Petra stuffs the envelope into her sweater.

DEE
Was that smart?

PETRA
No.

DEE
Okay.

PETRA
It was right.
